---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="In Prod" description="Real software, real constraints. Build processes and open source tooling from a small studio.">

  <div class="intro">
    <p class="section-label">Prima Digital — Studio Development Blog</p>
    <h1>In Prod</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Prima Digital documents what it builds: production SaaS, agentic products, and open source tooling for the community. vizstack is the open source release — a zero-install route and dependency visualizer for any file-based router codebase (Remix, Next.js, and more).</p>
    <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/vizstack" class="entry-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Clone on GitHub →</a>
  </div>

  <div class="prod-list">

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/22-vizstack-2" class="entry-title">VizStack 2.0</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">writing</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 17</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">We shipped VizStack as an open-source architecture visualizer. Then we wired Claude directly into the graph. It became an onboarding tool. We didn't plan that.</p>
      <a href="/posts/22-vizstack-2" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/21-v2-to-v3-learnings" class="entry-title">The V2 to V3 migration</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">writing</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 17</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">The real eval stack behind migrating a production LLM prompt on Shelf — a 32-check scoring rubric, a one-way runner, 54 adversarial payloads, Pydantic strict validation, and a hard rule about who can approve a prompt edit.</p>
      <a href="/posts/21-v2-to-v3-learnings" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/20-langflow-postgres" class="entry-title">Prototyping with Langflow and production data</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">writing</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 17</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">We used Langflow to sketch agentic patterns before hardcoding them in Python. We wired it to a local Postgres with production-level data. Here's what we learned and where we're still stuck.</p>
      <a href="/posts/20-langflow-postgres" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/19-long-prompting" class="entry-title">Prompts that run for hours</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">writing</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 17</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">What 250K context actually feels like in production. How we structure long-running prompt jobs on Shelf, what the industry is beginning to understand about this shift, and why we haven't really cracked it yet.</p>
      <a href="/posts/19-long-prompting" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/18-remix-route-visualizer" class="entry-title">Visualizing a Remix app</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">tooling</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 8</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">Why your app architecture is harder to hold in your head than it should be, and what we built to fix it — a route tree, an outlet chain view, and a cross-layer ecosystem map.</p>
      <a href="/posts/18-remix-route-visualizer" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/18-remix-route-visualizer" class="entry-title">vizstack</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">open source</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 8</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">vizstack is a zero-install CLI that turns any Remix or Next.js codebase into an interactive dependency map. Point it at a directory and it produces a single HTML file showing your routes, database, AI providers, and external APIs as a scrollable graph — hover any node to see what connects to it.</p>
      <a href="/tools/ecosystem-viz.html" class="viz-preview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <img src="/images/ecosystem-viz-preview.png" alt="Shelf ecosystem cross-layer dependency map — routes, database, AI layer, external APIs" class="viz-img" />
        <span class="viz-caption">Open interactive map →</span>
      </a>
      <div class="entry-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/jokeane9/vizstack" class="entry-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
        <a href="/posts/18-remix-route-visualizer" class="entry-link">How it was built →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/17-building-shelf" class="entry-title">Building Shelf</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">case-study</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 8</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">How we built a production Shopify competitor intelligence app end to end — the stack, the pipeline, the prompting mistakes, and what the discipline actually gave us.</p>
      <a href="/posts/17-building-shelf" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/17-building-shelf" class="entry-title">Shelf</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">live</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 8</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">Shelf is a Shopify app that gives merchants a daily briefing on what their competitors are doing — prices, inventory signals, stock levels. It crawls rival storefronts with Playwright, passes the signals through a four-layer AI pipeline, and surfaces the output inside the merchant's Shopify admin.</p>
      <a href="/posts/17-building-shelf" class="entry-link">How it was built →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="prod-entry">
      <div class="entry-meta">
        <a href="/posts/16-taste-judgment-and-the-ai-partner" class="entry-title">AI as Reliable Partners</a>
        <span class="entry-tag">philosophy</span>
        <span class="entry-date">May 4</span>
      </div>
      <p class="entry-desc">What humans bring to AI systems — taste, judgment, and technical intuition.</p>
      <a href="/posts/16-taste-judgment-and-the-ai-partner" class="entry-link">Read →</a>
    </div>

  </div>

</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .intro h1 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #888;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .prod-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .prod-entry {
    padding: 32px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .prod-entry:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .entry-title {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .entry-title:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .entry-tag {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    background: var(--border);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .entry-date {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-left: auto;
  }

  .entry-desc {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .entry-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .viz-preview {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .viz-preview:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

  .viz-img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .viz-caption {
    display: block;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: #0f0f0f;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-link {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: opacity 0.15s;
  }

  .entry-link:hover { opacity: 0.7; }

  /* Mobile */
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .intro h1 { font-size: 22px; }
    .entry-meta { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
    .entry-title { font-size: 15px; }
    .prod-entry { padding: 24px 0; }
    .viz-caption { font-size: 11px; }
  }
</style>
